  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5701.11 Law enforcement personnel",
  "priorExpiration": "2012-09-21",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5701.11 “Law enforcement personnel” means:\n\n(a) A sheriff or deputy sheriff of any county, a state police officer, a constable or police officer of any city or town, an official or employee of any jail or corrections institution, a conservation officer, or probation or parole officer; or\n\n(b) An individual authorized by the commissioner to access records as part of information system design, testing, implementation, or other related information system uses, pursuant to a contractual relationship with the department.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 5700) #6704, eff 3-3-98; ss by #8173, eff 9-21-04, EXPIRED: 9-21-12\n\nNew. #10208, eff 10-22-12; ss by #12132, eff 3-17-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5700.html"
